## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a concurrent, ordered pipeline with per-tenant semantics, backpressure, and dynamic worker changes; requires data structures (per-tenant queues + central dispatcher) and a test plan.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant in-order processing
- Bounded buffers and backpressure
- Dynamic worker resizing
- Late/out-of-order handling with reordering windows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal sketch showing per-tenant ordering with a map of queues
class TenantQueue {
  constructor() {
    this.expected = new Map();
    this.buffers = new Map();
  }
  enqueue(tenant, item) {
    const q = this.buffers.get(tenant) || [];
    q.push(item);
    this.buffers.set(tenant, q);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify backpressure and decide when to resize workers?
